  "rationale": "Block memoryDump:credentialAccess, fileServer:lateralMovement and codeRepo:collection. Blocking memoryDump kills dbLogin and apiToken, and therefore everything that depends on them: hypervisor, localAdmin, secretsManager, backupHost and serviceAccount. That leaves vaultRead with no reachable parent. With fileServer also blocked, shareMount and dbReplica lose all their remaining parents. codeRepo is blocked directly, so all four parents of the target are cut. Two blocks are not enough. Keeping codeRepo open would require blocking both printServer and monitoringHost, which uses both blocks and leaves fileServer to feed shareMount. So codeRepo itself must be blocked. The one remaining block must then be fileServer, because it has a direct path from sshKey, whose only parent is an unblockable entry. That still leaves vaultRead reachable via localAdmin or hypervisor."
 },
